Root cause:
The bug was caused by a memory leak in the `rtw_wx_set_enc_ext` function when an unsupported encryption algorithm was specified. The original code did not free the allocated `param` structure before returning an error, leading to a memory leak. The patch fixes this by ensuring that the `param` structure is freed in the error handling path when an unsupported algorithm is detected.
